  "body": "### Summary\nA flow that records the page's `hash_check` after its GET can overwrite a newer token if LOT-043's `adoptLogin` replaced the session's cookies and token meanwhile. The next POST then gets the bad-token answer (W17b). Found by the Fable review of LOT-051 (PR #263).\n\nScope\n- `TopicFlagFlow.swift:98` and `PostingFlow.swift:130`: compare the session identity (`userKey()`) before and after the request, and skip `updateHashCheck` if it changed. The alternative is a documented app-level rule of one flow at a time per session; pick one and record it in ARCHITECTURE or the LOT-043 spec.\n- Also, in `TopicFlagError.rejected`, replace \"nothing changed\" with \"by LOT-037's shape rule\": no addflag/delflag refusal is captured.\n\nAcceptance criteria: a test with a stub transport where a login is adopted between the GET and the token update shows that the fresher token is kept, and that the test fails without the change.",
